.TH BULK-RENAME 1 "2026-02-20" "ShellScript Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bulk-rename \- safely rename multiple files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bulk-rename
[\fIPATTERN\fR] [\fINEW_EXTENSION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renames files matching a pattern with a new extension.
Creates an undo log for safety.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B PATTERN
Glob pattern to match files (e.g., '*.txt')
.TP
.B NEW_EXTENSION
The new extension (e.g., '.md')
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B bulk-rename '*.txt' .md
Renames all .txt files to .md
.TP
.B bulk-rename 'IMG*.JPEG' .jpg
Renames IMG_001.JPEG to IMG_001.jpg
.SH SAFETY
Undo log created at .bulk-rename-TIMESTAMP.log
